course: dictionary
lesson: 9532
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. «The smallest bone in the body is the stirrup bone in the middle ear, about 3 millimetres long.» The clues are bone, body and middle ear, so stirrup here means a tiny bone.
explain: A horse rider uses a different stirrup: a metal loop on the side of the saddle for the rider's foot. Think of the sentence, not just the word. Is it about horses, battles, or your body? That tells you which meaning to choose.
explain: Check your choice by swapping in the meaning. «The three tiny bones, the hammer, anvil and stirrup, pass sound on.» Does "the three tiny bones, the hammer, anvil and metal loop" make sense? No, so the bone meaning is right.
fact: A stirrup is a metal loop that hangs on each side of a horse's saddle, for the rider to put their foot in.
fact: The stirrup is also a tiny bone in the middle ear, shaped like a stirrup.
fact: «The smallest bone, the stirrup in your ear, is smaller than a grain of rice.»
fact: The ear has three tiny bones: the hammer, anvil and stirrup. They pass sound on to the inner ear.
fact: Stirrups help riders keep their balance and stay on a horse, even in battle.
exercise: «The smallest bone in the body is the stirrup bone in the middle ear.» What is a stirrup here? | A loud sound | *A tiny bone in the middle ear | A metal loop for a horse rider's foot | A kind of horse
exercise: A rider puts their foot in the stirrup to keep their balance. Where is the stirrup? | In the body's longest bone | Under the horse's tail | Inside the ear | *On each side of a horse's saddle
exercise: «The three tiny bones called the hammer, anvil and stirrup pass sound on.» What do these bones do? | They hold up a horse's saddle | *They pass sound on to the inner ear | They are tools for building | They help a rider mount
test: Which bone is the smallest in the human body? | The anvil | *The stirrup in the middle ear | The femur | The hammer
test: Which word means the metal loop for a rider's foot? | *Stirrup | Femur | Cochlea | Saddle
exam: In «The stirrup is the smallest bone in your ear», what does stirrup mean? | A grain of rice | A metal loop for a horse rider | *A tiny bone in the middle ear | A kind of horse
